# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. The app RUNS WITHOUT THESE on mock
# data — only wire them when connecting to a real Supabase project.

# --- Client (browser, VITE_-prefixed, safe to expose: anon key is RLS-gated) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The zone the wall renders in. Set this rather than relying on the Pi's clock —
# Raspberry Pi OS ships on UTC unless someone ran raspi-config, and the whole
# wall would sit 7-8 hours off with nothing on screen to say why.
# VITE_HOME_TZ=America/Los_Angeles

# Dev only, stripped from production builds. Renders a local image as the wall's
# background photo so the 5B design can be judged with the layer it was composed
# around. Drop a file in dev-photos/ (gitignored, served only by the dev-only
# plugin in vite.config.ts) and point this at it. Real photos belong in the
# Supabase Storage `photos` bucket behind a signed URL, never in the repo —
# dev-photos/ is gitignored precisely so a family photo can't be committed.
# VITE_DEV_PHOTO_URL=/dev-photos/example.jpg

# --- Edge Function secrets (server-only; set via `supabase secrets set`) ---------
# NEVER put these in .env.local's VITE_ namespace — that ships them to the
# browser. An ICS URL is a bearer token: anyone holding it reads your calendar.
#
# CALENDAR_FEEDS is a JSON array of { url, source, color }. Each `source` MUST be
# unique — the per-source reconcile uses it as the identity of a calendar.
# CALENDAR_FEEDS=[{"url":"https://calendar.google.com/.../basic.ics","source":"google_cal","color":"hsl(42 60% 62%)"}]
#
# PEOPLE maps a calendar title prefix ("Alex: Swim class") to a colour. Keep it
# in step with `people` in src/config/family.ts — `peopleMap()` there emits
# exactly this shape.
# PEOPLE={"Alex":"hsl(208 66% 72%)","Sam":"hsl(44 74% 56%)"}
#
# Ingest's counterpart to VITE_HOME_TZ: anchors all-day events and any TZID that
# can't be resolved from a VTIMEZONE. Keep the two in sync.
# HOME_TZ=America/Los_Angeles
#
# Where to fetch weather for. Round these — two decimals is ~1km, which is
# plenty for a forecast and vague enough not to be your street.
# WEATHER_LAT=37.77
# WEATHER_LON=-122.42
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is injected into Edge Functions automatically.
